# Inline union annotation in function signature: [@[Integer String] expr]
# resolves as Union(Int, Str) — two positional type entries produce a union.
# A function that returns @[or Integer String] can return either Int or String.
[
  to-int-or-str: [fn@[or Integer String] [let n@Integer]
    [if [= n 0] 0 "nonzero"]]
  v1: [to-int-or-str 0]
  v2: [to-int-or-str 1]
]
=== out
Dict({"to-int-or-str": Function(n), "v1": Int(0), "v2": String("nonzero")})
